                <pb facs="0594" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6213: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-30T16:00:00+08:00">July 30, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 30—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>419. Reuter under London date line July 29th states rumors persist China seeks
                    20,000,000 pounds loan for economic development from Great Britain, France,
                    Belgium and Japan. Also reports Japanese press extending feelers for revival
                    Anglo-Japanese friendship. Repeated to Peiping, by mail to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
